{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786481692,"nonce":"/p5G1AMirHNXdh2BKJUEDbDJbNc=","title":"**What is wrong.** `web/src/index.css`'s `@theme inline` block (`:12-71`) maps **every** colour the design system owns — 15 chrome tokens, 24 state tokens across six states, 7 chart tokens — plus `--font-sans` (`:13`) and `--font-mono` (`:15`). It defines no `--text-*` and no `--radius-*`. The consequence is that font size and corner radius are the two axes with no vocabulary, and every component invents a px literal in a bracket: **285 `text-[Npx]` across 32 files** and **57 `rounded-[Npx]`**. Not one named size utility (`text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-base`, …) appears anywhere in `web/src`.","message":"**The demonstration.** An unnamed scale already exists de facto, and the histogram shows it clearly. Font size resolves to 7 distinct values: `11px`×159, `12px`×75, `13px`×23, `10px`×20, `14px`×4, `18px`×2, `15px`×2 — the first four are the real scale, carrying 277 of 285 occurrences, and the trailing three are 8 occurrences across three values. Radius resolves to `4px`×27, `3px`×26 and then 4 stragglers across three values: `6px`×2, `8px`×1, `2px`×1. A 26/27 split between `3px` and `4px` with no rule for which is which is not two tiers; it is one tier written two ways. `index.css:95` adds a third instance of the same decision as a raw `border-radius: 3px` in the `:focus-visible` rule, so the focus ring's corner and a component's corner agree by coincidence rather than by reference.\n\nThe density is concentrated: `features/settings/TuningSection.tsx` carries 64 bracket literals across both axes, `features/alerts/detail/RuleDrift.tsx` 37, `features/settings/PoliciesSection.tsx` 23, `components/ui/primitives.tsx` 20. That last one is the shared primitives module, which means the components meant to be the vocabulary are themselves spelling it out in px.\n\n**Why it matters — and this is a proposal, not a violation.** SPEC §M is silent on type and radius. `docs/design/SPEC.md:4858-4869` (§M.3, the rules that survive the aesthetic) names px in exactly two places and neither is a scale: U2 sets contrast tiers at *\"≥ 24 px / ≥ 19 px-bold\"*, and U6 sets *\"row height 36 px comfortable / 28 px compact\"*. §M.7 (`:5071-5079`) lists the enforcement tests, and all of them are colour: `contrast.test.ts`, `tokens.test.ts`, `TestNoStateHueInChrome`, `TestSlackPaletteUnchanged`, the axe contrast run. ADR 0012 likewise discusses only the four-token state sets. `CONTEXT.md:255-262` restates the two tiers as a colour rule. So nothing in the binding documents is being broken here, and the ticket should not pretend otherwise.\n\nWhat is true is narrower and still worth fixing: the system has one axis with names and enforcement, and two axes with 342 hand-written literals and no way to tell a deliberate value from a typo. The three radius stragglers are almost certainly meant to be one of the two real tiers, and there is no test or grep that would ever say so.\n\n**Where.** `web/src/index.css:12-71` (the `@theme inline` block that stops at colour), `web/src/index.css:95` (the raw `border-radius: 3px`), `web/src/design/tokens.css` (colour only, no dimension tokens), and the four densest consumers: `features/settings/TuningSection.tsx`, `features/alerts/detail/RuleDrift.tsx`, `features/settings/PoliciesSection.tsx`, `components/ui/primitives.tsx`.\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** `@theme inline` defines a type scale covering the four real sizes and a radius scale covering the two real tiers, every `text-[Npx]` and `rounded-[Npx]` is replaced by its named utility with the strays resolved to a deliberate tier, `index.css:95` references the radius token, and — because this axis is currently unenforceable — a lint or a `design/` test rejects a new bracket literal on either axis. If the scale is adopted, SPEC §M and §M.7 are amended in the same commit per the §N procedure.","files":null}]}